    "summary": "I built a single-cell storage box. It's a full hex base with a full-depth bin inside and a full cover on top as the lid. All six open side faces have solid end caps, so it's closed on every side. The lid shuts with magnets: the parts list includes 6 Ø5×1 mm neodymium disc magnets and 6 steel BBs that they hold onto. Those were already included when I fitted the cover, and trying to switch magnets on said it would change nothing. check_build found no issues and the collision check is clear. That's 12 printed parts, about 629 g and 857 minutes (roughly 14 hours) of printing. The configurator only checks fit, so it can't say how strongly the magnets will hold.",
